  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for Renewable Energy in Aquaculture (CEREA) - WorldFish</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of climate-adapted energy-based innovations and practices in Egyptian aquaculture.
Establishment of a Centre for Renewable Energy in Aquaculture. 
Producers and processors to get better access to renewable energy solutions.
The project harnesses science and technical expertise from multiple institutions to contribute to climate adaptation and mitigation efforts in several ways. The project will only pilot and scale renewable energy innovations with demonstrable climate resilience benefits to the aquaculture value chain. These innovations will be used for climate adaptation and environmental sustainability within Egyptian aquaculture. It is also expected that the innovations promoted by the project will make more efficient use of natural resources, reduce waste and loss, reduce reliance on fossil fuels, lower the carbon footprint of food production, and increase the environmental benefits obtainable from aquaculture.</narrative>
  </description>
